Stable signing identity
=======================

Every rebuild changes an ad-hoc signature, so macOS sees a different app and
drops its Screen Recording and Accessibility grants. That failure looks exactly
like the app being broken, and it has cost this build several rounds.

Installing a self-signed identity once fixes it permanently — make.sh picks it
up automatically and the permissions then survive every rebuild:

    security import "$HOME/Claude 1/ambient/signing/ambient.p12" \
      -k ~/Library/Keychains/login.keychain-db -P ambient -T /usr/bin/codesign

The passphrase is "ambient". An empty one fails: macOS rejects the PKCS#12 MAC
that OpenSSL writes by default, which reads as "wrong password".

Then rebuild (./make.sh) and grant the two permissions one last time.

The certificate is self-signed and local — it is not a developer account, and
it does nothing beyond giving this app a stable identity on this machine.
